{"schema":"landfall.snapshot/1","id":"osdr_cmp","adapter":"osdr","title":"Inspiration4 crew comprehensive metabolic panel (OSD-575), with per-sample lab reference ranges","source":{"publisher":"NASA Open Science Data Repository (OSDR)","name":"OSD-575: SpaceX Inspiration4 Blood Serum Metabolic Panel and Immune/Cardiac Cytokine Arrays (Comprehensive Metabolic Panel and Multiplex)","url":"https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-575","access_urls":["https://osdr.nasa.gov/osdr/data/osd/files/575","https://osdr.nasa.gov/osdr/data/osd/meta/575","https://osdr.nasa.gov/geode-py/ws/studies/OSD-575/download?source=datamanager&file=LSDS-8_Comprehensive_Metabolic_Panel_CMP.upload_SUBMITTED.csv","https://osdr.nasa.gov/geode-py/ws/studies/OSD-575/download?source=datamanager&file=LSDS-8_Comprehensive_Metabolic_Panel_CMP_TRANSFORMED.csv"],"license":"not stated in the OSDR API response; the files are publicly released (OSDR file records 'restricted': false). Check the OSDR study page before reuse.","citation":"NASA Open Science Data Repository (OSDR). OSD-575: SpaceX Inspiration4 Blood Serum Metabolic Panel and Immune/Cardiac Cytokine Arrays (Comprehensive Metabolic Panel and Multiplex). Study version 3, submitted 2022-12-05, publicly released 2024-05-14. https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-575 (no dataset DOI is stated in the OSDR metadata). Investigators listed by OSDR: Christopher Mason (principal investigator); Eliah Overbey (co-investigator); Kirill Grigorev (formal analysis role); Theodore Nelson (formal analysis role). Publications listed by OSDR: The Space Omics and Medical Atlas (SOMA) and international astronaut biobank (doi:10.1038/s41586-024-07639-y); Collection of Biospecimens from the Inspiration4 Mission Establishes the Standards for the Space Omics and Medical Atlas (SOMA) (doi:10.1038/s41467-024-48806-z); CAMbank: SST Field Processing v1 (doi:10.17504/protocols.io.81wgbxxo1lpk/v1)."},"retrieved_at":"2026-11-14T13:26:23Z","coverage":{"start":"2021-06-16T00:00:00Z","stop":"2022-03-31T00:00:00Z","cadence":null},"freshness":{"kind":"historical","stale_after":null},"provenance":"measured","caveats":["Inspiration4 was a ~3-day civilian low-Earth-orbit flight (OSDR metadata: mission 2021-09-16 to 2021-09-18) with n=4 crew. These files contain NO in-flight samples: only pre-flight L-92/L-44/L-3 and post-flight R+1/R+45/R+82/R+194 (the OSDR study description says 'The crew collected biospecimen samples before, during, and after flight', but no in-flight sample is in these files). These files provide real laboratory reference ranges and a real post-flight recovery shape; they are NOT a model of a long-duration exploration mission and must not be presented as one.","within_own_range is an OBSERVATION (value inside the reference range the laboratory printed for that same sample, bounds inclusive; one-sided ranges compare one bound), not an alert, not a diagnosis and not a NASA threshold. NASA publishes no numeric in-flight alert threshold for these analytes.","Timepoint dates are nominal and derived (label offset from the OSDR mission start for L-, from the mission end for R+); actual collection timestamps are not in these files.","CMP: reference ranges are per SAMPLE and change within a subject (C003 recorded as F). LANDFALL reproduces the range the lab printed for each sample and does not correct it; never collapse them to one range per analyte or per subject. Creatinine C003: 0.6-1.35 at L-92, L-44, L-3; 0.5-1.1 at R+1, R+45, R+82, R+194 | Calcium (serum) C003: 8.6-10.3 at L-92, L-44, L-3; 8.6-10.2 at R+1, R+45, R+82, R+194 | Alkaline phosphatase (ALP) C003: 36-130 at L-92, L-44, L-3; 31-125 at R+1, R+45, R+82, R+194 | AST C003: 10-40 at L-92, L-44, L-3; 10-30 at R+1, R+45, R+82, R+194 | ALT C003: 9-46 at L-92, L-44, L-3; 6-29 at R+1, R+45, R+82, R+194","OSD-575's study description lists serum timepoints L-92 to R+82 only, but the CMP files also contain R+194 for all four crew; it is included.","Serum calcium is a blood concentration, not urinary calcium excretion. OSD-656 (the Inspiration4 urine study) contains no urine chemistry at all, so no OSDR Inspiration4 file can drive the bone -> renal-stone case as urine data.","eGFR is reported by the lab in two race-based variants with a one-sided range (RANGE_MAX 'N/A'); both are reproduced exactly as published, not endorsed.","BUN/creatinine ratio is 'NA' in most samples as published (and one row is absent); those are null here, never imputed.","ALSDA TRANSFORMED CMP file: the ALT and AST upper limits are named 'alt_max_units_per_liter' / 'ast_max_units_per_liter' (no 'range_'); this adapter classifies every column or fails, so those limits cannot be dropped silently."],"data":{"study":{"id":"OSD-575","title":"SpaceX Inspiration4 Blood Serum Metabolic Panel and Immune/Cardiac Cytokine Arrays (Comprehensive Metabolic Panel and Multiplex)","version":3,"submission_date":"2022-12-05","public_release_date":"2024-05-14","landing_url":"https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-575","dataset_doi":null,"publications":[{"title":"The Space Omics and Medical Atlas (SOMA) and international astronaut biobank","doi":"10.1038/s41586-024-07639-y","pmid":null},{"title":"Collection of Biospecimens from the Inspiration4 Mission Establishes the Standards for the Space Omics and Medical Atlas (SOMA)","doi":"10.1038/s41467-024-48806-z","pmid":null},{"title":"CAMbank: SST Field Processing v1","doi":"10.17504/protocols.io.81wgbxxo1lpk/v1","pmid":null}],"files":[{"name":"LSDS-8_Comprehensive_Metabolic_Panel_CMP.upload_SUBMITTED.csv","url":"https://osdr.nasa.gov/geode-py/ws/studies/OSD-575/download?source=datamanager&file=LSDS-8_Comprehensive_Metabolic_Panel_CMP.upload_SUBMITTED.csv","bytes":25275,"sha256":"dab247eb794edab59aaaa683c85fd1f2dbf4ae3684872739338e10ead4192a0c","osdr_category":"Comprehensive Metabolic Panel","osdr_subdirectory":"Original Submitted","osdr_date_updated":"2024-05-15"},{"name":"LSDS-8_Comprehensive_Metabolic_Panel_CMP_TRANSFOR